Reverend Ezekiel Grimm is the founder and spiritual leader of [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/Haven/index|Haven]] and the [[Org/Althane/Church of the Thirteenth Realm|Church of the Thirteenth Realm]]

Grimm is a young-looking [[Bestiary/Visitors from Beyond#Kitsune|elven]] male with slicked-back black hair and thick-framed glasses. He has a glowing halo and set of white, feathered wings as is common with the members of the Church of the Thirteenth Realm. He is short statured and soft spoken, but can still command a room when he needs to.

Grimm ruled [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/index|the Gulch]] as a miracle-maker: he and his acolytes seemed to make food from nothing, to bless their people and grant wishes. The truth was a long partnership with the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]] of Oresk and its head, [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]]: together they drew power from the corpse of the Thessian Beast beneath [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/Haven/index|Haven]], whose blood seeps into the ground. A dead god still dreams, and Grimm made things in the Beast's dream and brought them into the waking world. He meant to make a utopia of Althane by brainwashing everyone within the dream to be eternally happy and then spreading the dream over the globe. The Weft gathered allies and made war on him, and he died. With him died the miracle of Haven, and its people were left stranded in the Gulch without food or shelter.
